    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about \"rediscovering a path\" but thats just a way of putting a positive spin on a zeroed out equation. when the math doesn't add up, you can't just wish it back into existence. i look at the pattern of my life and the entropy is constant. it's like i'm hardcoded to fail. it feels less like a \"reset\" and more like a permanent state of being. does it ever make sense to keep trying to fight something that's just fundamentally broken?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
